* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #30, Part of #16)
* POST-LAYOUT open-loop VCO frequency-vs-VCTRL sweep at a fixed band-select
* code and PVT corner -- the parasitic-annotated twin of
* ../../sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table/testbench/tb_vco_kvco.sp.tmpl, deliberately
* kept line-for-line comparable to it so the only difference between the two
* campaigns' numbers is the extracted interconnect R/C.
*
* ../run.sh sweeps @VCTRL@/@B0V@/@B1V@ over the SAME matrix that campaign
* ratified (3 PVT bundles x 4 band codes x 5 VCTRL points) and substitutes
* @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib: mos_tt/mos_ss/mos_ff), @CORNER_RES@
* (cornerRES.lib: res_typ/res_wcs/res_bcs) and @TEMP@ (degC) identically.
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ are substituted because ngspice's .lib parser does not
* expand environment variables (issue #43).
*
* The DUT is `pll_vco`, the subcircuit `klt extract --deck sg13cmos5l
* --parasitics --pdk ihp-sg13cmos5l` produced from the ROUTED GDS of layout
* record 20260830-204105-457cf5b -- 44 devices, 33 nets, 170 parasitic
* resistors and 33 net-to-substrate + 311 net-to-net coupling capacitors, all
* from klt's curated sg13cmos5l metal coefficients. `vco_inst.spice` is
* generated by ../run.sh from the extracted subcircuit's own pin list rather
* than transcribed by hand, because the extracted cell exposes every internal
* net as a pin and a hand-written port order would be a silent-miswire risk.
*
* Not modelled here, and not claimed: XCDECAP. The routed cell has no
* `cap_cmomi` drawn (44 of 45 schematic devices; see layout/sg13cmos5l-pll/
* README.md), and the schematic-side campaign strips XCDECAP for its own
* stated reason (an ideal VDD source makes it unobservable). Both sides of
* this comparison therefore exclude it, for two different but compatible
* reasons -- neither side makes any claim about XCDECAP.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include vco_pex.spice
.include vco_inst.spice

Vvctrl vctrl 0 dc @VCTRL@
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@
Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

* The extracted netlist declares its own `.GLOBAL vsubs` and ties it to
* ground only through klt's 1e12-ohm DC tie. Every extracted net-to-ground
* parasitic capacitor returns to that node, so leaving it at 1e12 ohms would
* leave those capacitors driving a floating node and silently cancel most of
* the loading this record exists to measure. Held hard at 0 V, which is what
* the substrate physically is here and what the schematic-side testbench
* already does for its own `sub!`.
Vsubs vsubs 0 dc 0

* Same symmetry break as the schematic-level testbench, applied to the same
* ring node -- which the extracted cell exposes as a top-level pin, so this
* is `v(ring1)` rather than `v(xvco.ring1)`.
.ic v(ring1)=0.5

.tran 20p 30n

.control
run
meas tran per1 trig v(clk) val=1.65 rise=3 targ v(clk) val=1.65 rise=4
print per1
.endc
.end
